glare:
Of my veiled bride in her maiden bloom;
Keeps she watch through glare and through gloom,
Watch for me asleep and awake?'--

gladly:
Softly you told of loves that went before,--
Of clinging arms, of kisses gladly given;
Luxuriously clean of heart once more,

Out of the wound new joy will start;
Only love proudly and gladly and well,
Though love be heaven or love be hell.

glaring:
Glad to leave far below the clanging city;
Looking far downward to the glaring street
Gaudy with light, yet tired with many feet,

glaze:
Until late Summer's wane;
But now that frost begins to glaze
How should one love again?

gladness:
With gifts of thy opulent giving we come;
O source of our manifold gladness, we hail thee,
We praise thee, O Prithvi, with cymbal and drum.

gladder:
That paddles in a halcyon sea;
My heart is gladder than all these
Because my love is come to me.

gladiators:
Loud the clashing sabres rang;
When between the gladiators
All unarmed a hermit sprang.
